*** Add File:README_SECURITY_AND_COMPLIANCE.md
+# Aegis — Security, Compliance & Availability Patch
+
+This patch adds enforcement and runbook artifacts to reduce the attack and compliance surface:
+
+- CI job to verify cosign signatures for all images referenced in k8s manifests (.github/workflows/ci_cosign_verify.yml). Fails PRs that reference unsigned/unsigned images (relies on COSIGN_PUB_KEY secret).
+- Gatekeeper ConstraintTemplate + Constraint to require CI-added mcp.provenance annotations on Deployments (k8s/gatekeeper/*). This lets CI add provenance metadata (cosign/Rekor) and admission enforce presence before allowing promotion to staging/production.
+- HA ValidatingWebhook deployment + HPA and ValidatingWebhookConfiguration sample (k8s/webhooks/*). Use failurePolicy Ignore for staging, Fail for production as a fail-open/fail-closed strategy.
+- Presidio adapter Deployment + Gatekeeper constraint requiring presidio.redacted=true annotation for resources labeled data.contains_pii=true (k8s/presidio/*, k8s/privacy/*) + a takedown test script (services/privacy/takedown_test.sh).
+- Drift detector CronJob and a small helper to open A2A approvals when drift is high (k8s/monitoring/drift-cronjob.yaml, services/monitoring/drift_detector_alert_to_a2a.py).
+- Milvus HA StatefulSet, backup CronJob and a backup script (k8s/milvus/*, services/milvus/backup.sh). Replace placeholders with provider-specific backup/restore tooling.
+- Runbooks for webhook failover and Milvus restore (runbooks/*).
+- RuntimeClass (kata) and seccomp ConfigMap + sandbox NetworkPolicy to reduce blast radius (k8s/runtimeclasses/*, k8s/security/*).
+- Image allowlist via Gatekeeper (k8s/gatekeeper/constrainttemplate-image-allowlist.yaml, k8s/gatekeeper/constraint-image-allowlist.yaml) and example allowlist configmap (k8s/security/image-allowlist-configmap.yaml).
+
+Operator notes:
+- Replace placeholder images and secrets (cosign public key, webhook TLS secret, S3 bucket, etc.) before enabling in production.
+- Install Gatekeeper and cert-manager; deploy webhook with CA bundle populated from cert-manager; run webhook in audit (failurePolicy=Ignore) for 48–72h and remediate violations before switching to Fail.
+- Ensure Presidio adapter has network access to ingestion endpoints and the KMS key for encrypting originals.
+- Configure drift detector and A2A endpoints; review and tune thresholds.
+- Swap Milvus sample StatefulSet for your Helm-backed production chart and ensure backups are integrated with your storage provider.
+- Apply RuntimeClass and ensure nodes are provisioned with kata runtime or gVisor handlers and PREEMPT_RT images for RT workloads.
+
